1
00:00:00,632 --> 00:00:02,882
(Howard:)When the Mars rover
started pulling to the left...

2
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:08,761
...I performed a front-end alignment
from 62 million miles away.

3
00:00:17,941 --> 00:00:19,981
(Howard:)No, that baby's broken.

4
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:23,817
LEONARD:
Come on, guys, push.

5
00:00:23,988 --> 00:00:28,198
HOWARD: If I push any harder,
I'm gonna give birth to my colon.

6
00:00:28,368 --> 00:00:30,118
RAJESH:
I can't feel my fingers. Hurry up.

7
00:00:30,286 --> 00:00:33,626
(Sheldon:)It's the same amount of work,
no matter how fast you go. Basic physics.

8
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:35,000
RAJESH: Sheldon.
- Yeah?

9
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:39,506
RAJESH: If my fingers ever work again,
I've got a job for the middle one.

10
00:00:40,213 --> 00:00:41,713
- Oh, hey, guys.
- Hi, Penny.

11
00:00:41,881 --> 00:00:42,921
[RAJESH AND HOWARD SCREAM]

12
00:00:45,468 --> 00:00:47,348
(Leonard(letting go of time machine, as does Sheldon):)Take a break, guys.

13
00:00:48,179 --> 00:00:51,519
- What are you doing?
- Just moving something upstairs.

14
00:00:51,849 --> 00:00:56,189
- What is it?
- Just, you know, a time machine.

15
00:00:56,771 --> 00:00:58,731
(Penny:)Okay, neat.
But I really gotta get to work.

